---
import StanBannerDoodle from '../../assets/stan-banner-doodle.svg';
import StanBanner from '../../assets/stan-banner.svg';
import CenterContainer from '../../components/CenterContainer.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DemoVideo from '../../components/DemoVideo.astro';
import Paragraph from '../../components/Paragraph.astro';
import ProjectBanner from '../../components/ProjectBanner.astro';
import Spacer from '../../components/Spacer.astro';
import Layout from '../../layout/Layout.astro';
import { asset } from '../../utils/base-url';
---

<Layout>
	<CenterContainer>
		<ProjectBanner doodleId="stanDoodle">
			<StanBanner slot="logo" />
			<StanBannerDoodle slot="doodle" />
		</ProjectBanner>
		<ContentCard title="My Work At Stan">
			<div class="pad">
				<Paragraph heading="Over Four Years,Building Australia's Streaming Platform">
					For the past four years, I've been part of the six person CTV team behind <b>Stan</b>,
					Australia's largest homegrown streaming service.
					<br />
					I maintain the core TV app running on 175+ platforms serving 1.6M+ users across smart TVs, game
					consoles, and set top boxes.
					<br />
					From the 2024 Olympics to daily binge watching, every stream on TV runs through code I've written.
				</Paragraph>
				<Spacer />
				<DemoVideo
					src={asset('stan.mp4')}
					poster={asset('stan-poster.jpg')}
					width={1280}
					height={720}
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="pad">
				<Paragraph heading="Open Source,Awards, and Big Wins">
					Three of my fixes ship in Google's Shaka Player. All three started the same way: something
					felt slow on a TV that came out a decade ago.
					<br />
					First was the <a
						href="https://github.com/shaka-project/shaka-player/pull/9066"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener"
						class="inline-link">HLS parser</a
					>, redoing the same work on every segment. Lifting it out of the loop took manifest parsing
					from roughly 1600ms to 400ms. That one won the Nine Digital Annual Award for "No Stone Left
					Unturned", one of only four given each year.
					<br />
					The second was quieter. Shaka built a <a
						href="https://github.com/shaka-project/shaka-player/pull/10501"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener"
						class="inline-link">fresh error object on every abortable operation</a
					> whether anything had gone wrong or not, and building an error means building a stack trace.
					That is not free. Deleting work that never needed doing shortened garbage collection pauses on
					old webviews.
					<br />
					The third was a <a
						href="https://github.com/shaka-project/shaka-player/pull/10506"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener"
						class="inline-link">leak</a
					>. XHR handlers kept hold of their requests and response buffers long after the request
					finished, and the collectors in Chrome 38 era browsers never worked it out. Releasing them
					took the listener count from 306 to 36 over a minute of playback.
					<br />
					Closer to home, I lead device performance initiatives. One brought 2015+ legacy devices onto
					the latest app version and grew platform coverage by 30%, and two more are in flight right now.
					And during the 2024 Olympics I rebuilt core navigation, steadied the app, and improved analytics
					and reporting under the highest traffic event of our year.
				</Paragraph>
			</div>
			<div class="pad">
				<Paragraph heading="The Tech Stack">
					Built with React, TypeScript, and Redux running across Tizen, WebOS, WebMAF and dozens of
					other platforms.
					<br />
					Webpack handles the heavy lifting for 175+ device configurations each with unique quirks and
					limitations. Targeting devices all the way down to Chrome 38 and Safari 7.
					<br />
					I've built custom internal tooling around native tooling gaps, creating a unified dev experience
					across every platform.
					<br />
					It's the kind of infrastructure work that doesn't ship features but makes shipping features
					possible.
				</Paragraph>
			</div>
			<div class="pad">
				<Paragraph heading="Systems, Tools, and Architecture">
					<b
						>I help drive the architecture behind 175+ platforms, and build the foundational
						libraries that these platforms rely on.</b
					>
					<br />
					Design system, analytics, player bugs, performance, platform quirks: if it lands on constrained
					TV hardware, it lands on me. I refactored our monolithic codebase into a modular, testable
					monorepo and designed cross device testing pipelines that unblocked QA.
					<br />
					From remote logging and debugging tools to custom runtimes, I build the tooling that keeps a
					multi platform app stable and devs happy.
				</Paragraph>
			</div>
			<div class="pad">
				<Paragraph heading="Optimisations at Scale">
					<b
						>My performance work goes deep into ancient browsers and hardware limits. Every fix is
						backed by profiling data, not guesswork.</b
					>
					<br />
					Some of my work includes diagnosing and eliminating redundant React renders, optimising garbage
					collection (yep), forcing hardware decoding and batching network requests between user interactions
					to name a few.
					<br />
					By engineering custom GPU optimised animation hooks that devs adhere to, I stopped layout thrashing
					animations getting into production and ensured smooth UI across even the oldest of platforms.
				</Paragraph>
			</div>
			<div class="pad">
				<Paragraph heading="Team Culture">
					<b>Lifting the standard around me is part of the work, not a side project.</b>
					<br />
					I actively mentor junior developers, host organisation wide tech talks and represent our platform's
					hardware constraints in Stan's internal design system teams.
					<br />
					Championing a strong team culture helped us take home the award for Best Teamwork at Nine Digital's
					annual hackathon.
				</Paragraph>
			</div>
			<Spacer />
		</ContentCard>
		<Spacer triple />
	</CenterContainer>

	<style>
		.inline-link {
			color: var(--text);
			text-decoration: underline;
			text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
			text-underline-offset: 3px;
			transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
		}

		.pad {
			padding: 20px;
		}

		.inline-link:hover {
			opacity: 0.7;
		}
	</style>
</Layout>
